  "articleSummary": "**Core Thesis:** The AI security threat is not a single sci-fi breakthrough, but the compounding multiplication of two ordinary curves—agent endurance (task length) and breadth (orchestrated sub-agents)—supercharged by \"LLMjacking,\" where attackers use stolen credentials so victims unknowingly pay for the malicious compute.\n\n**Key Technologies & Concepts:** Autonomous AI agents, multi-agent orchestrators (e.g., Claude Code, METR task-horizon metrics), and LLMjacking (stealing cloud credentials to execute unpaid LLM workloads).\n\n**Tone & Framing:** Pragmatic, analytical, and urgent warning wrapped in a recurring *Terminator* (\"absolutely will not stop\") framing device, shifting the terror from sci-fi robots to relentless, automated billing meters and swarm economics. \n\n**Intended Audience:** Software engineering teams, cloud security professionals, and technical leadership skeptical of current AI agent threat models.",
